==English==

===Etymology===
From {{term|cat}} + {{term|waul}}, {{term|wawl}}, to [[cry]] as a [[cat]].

===Pronunciation===
*Cat"er*waul
*{{audio|en-us-caterwaul.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Verb===
{{WikiSaurus-link|argument}}
{{en-verb}}

# {{intransitive}} To [[cry]] as cats in [[rutting]] time; to make a [[harsh]], [[offensive]] noise.
# To have a noisy argument, like cats.

